      "side": 0,
      "message": "Benchmark says it doesn\u0027t matter?\nhttps://screenshot.googleplex.com/3Tmm5GhGcqP7bYG\n\nPlease be aware that I have low faith in this benchmark. At smaller sample sizes (--ms\u003d5000) it was wildly unreliable. I was unable to get consistent results unless I waited at least 15 seconds between runs, probably due to thermal effects. There was tons of noise but no signal that implicated this CL in any performance delta.\n\nAt larger sizes (--ms\u003d15000) with the computer running cool (wait for low fan noise) it seems to have stabilized on a median of 14 - 14.4 µs regardless of which branch I pick.",
